  "id": 203712401035242,
  "uuid": "e7efba44-87ca-4461-a996-36da4ca2b400",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "014470b3-c9ce-4363-3393-bff127fbc98f",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "817e604d-9fa9-f426-ce26-1151a10904f0",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr. Azam Ali, Consultant Ophthalmologist and Head of Ophthalmology Section at AKUH will be giving a presentation on \"Diabetic and other Eye Problems and their Latest Treatment\".",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr. Ali did his MBBS, with honors, from Aga Khan University Karachi, FRCS from Glasgow, Edinburgh and FRCOphth (UK). He got training from and Eye Hospital in London and specialized in Vitreo-Retina from Moorfields Eye Hospital.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The programme will include a question and answer session in which participants would be encouraged to ask questions.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Aga Khan University (AKU) is part of Aga Khan Development Network, a group of private international development agencies, founded by His Highness the Aga Khan, which works in the developing countries of Asia and Africa.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The University Hospital provides high quality services to all segments of the population. Over 70% of the patients come from low to middle income areas.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Since the inception of the Hospital's Patient Welfare Programme in 1986, Dhs 67.3 million has been spent benefiting over 203,000 needy patients.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "AKUH Representative office was inaugurated in May 2002 in Dubai. It is located at the Oud Metha Office Complex, it provides convenience and easy accessibility to AKUH's high-quality, cost-effective services to patients in the United Arab Emirates.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
